  "decision": "CLOSE_FALSE_POSITIVE",
  "confidence": 0.95,
  "rationale": "The customer's date of birth (2002-08-14) conflicts with the listed party's date of birth (1977-02-24) at day precision, and nationality (DE) does not match listed nationality (LB). No document identifiers overlap. The screener detected risk signals in the customer note, but both have grounded: false and the note does not meet documentary evidence standards (missing check reference, document number). Per the false positive definition, free text that is not documentary is a claim and does not prevent closure when structured fields meet the definition. The comparison confirms false_positive is true.",
  "what_would_change": [
    "Documentary evidence in the customer note meeting the standard (check reference, document number, date) that resolves the risk signals",
    "A matching date of birth for the listed party to the day (2002-08-14) would make true_match true, leading to ESCALATE_L2 or RECOMMEND_BLOCK",
    "A matching nationality or citizenship for the listed party (DE) would strengthen the match",
    "A matching document identifier between customer and listed party"
  ],
